This is the cleaned dataset used in the Turbine Health Monitoring & Failure Forecasting project.
The goal of this project is to predict wind turbine failures before they happen using machine learning.

About the File : 
File name: Data_Science_Cleaned.csv
Total rows: 9,000
Total columns: 17
Missing values: None (sensor columns are fully clean)


Out of 9,000 records:
  Label     Count    Percentage 
No Failure  7,848      87.2%
Failure     1,152      12.8%

Among the 1,152 failures, the fault types are:

Fault Type  Count
Gearbox     586
Blades      314
Generator   252

Only 12.8% of records are failures. This is realistic — turbines don't fail often.
But it means a model that always predicts "No Failure" would be 87% accurate and completely wrong for the job.
